527e4a36e44495d56eb211b96b79aa" "q-32321/selection/21e249ce11d2b353c98e6f393dab39860a6b28d257d5c8ab71564f01e5f47bd7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-32321" :question/id #uuid "84dd1552-3f60-57dc-aae2-e0aaa6ebc5f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-32321" :question/problem "Consider the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}].$ Find $f(A)$ if $f(X)={X}^{2}-3X+1.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we rewrite the polynomial, interpreting any constants as multiples of the identity matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(X) & ={X}^{2}-3X+1 \\\\  & ={X}^{2}-3X+I\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find $f(A)={A}^{2}-3A+I.$\n\nLet's calculate ${A}^{2}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{2} & =A\\cdot A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 15\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can evaluate $f(A):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(A) & ={A}^{2}-3A+I \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 15\\end{aligned}]-3[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10 & 6 \\\\ 1 & 15\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 18 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}10-(-6)+1 & 6-18 \\\\ 1-3 & 15-9+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}17 & -12 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-32321/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "61443225-bc08-5d36-a603-3a1d7e392a98"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-32321"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130582/selection/c8f3bfcac38a4fe284fc4d8b7a547c56e06dee638bbe51e027f056152e402738" :answer/id #uuid "4f845142-dd21-541c-8588-0d3cbe9ded3d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\e