:question/math-academy-id "q-130582" :question/problem "If $U=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]$, then ${U}^{3}=$" :question/worked-solution "First, to find ${U}^{2},$ we multiply $U$ by itself:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{2} & =U\\cdot U \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${U}^{3}={U}^{2}\\cdot U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{U}^{3} & ={U}^{2}\\cdot U \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}8 & 24 \\\\ -24 & -8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-130582/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e970fe-cff8-50e3-9b94-67ad97b03da7"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-130582"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-130684/selection/116ba511f78f3ed888236c80aa0db20008860383f2b47eb517f411d99b4bfe21" :answer/id #uuid "bc48d304-5608-59c0-bf0f-212e59aadf15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130684/selection/aa29ed5fd4b84ed96bf8932f0bcf3e8893d304f3e0be2e111668a3cf2390e89d" :answer/id #uuid "2e646f1d-ceb6-5b3c-b5f0-781f2f09a1e2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130684/selection/51319135bacd0b831c93b8d34d6bd0347fe1851699cf2ee841cacf54ab3cb851" :answer/id #uuid "c83e22f8-b3de-5a66-95b9-bd18ffb596c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-130684/selection/04df0a3ed643683ef581aae8a76cee400e540125111f015413c03e0b2926aa21" :answer/id #uuid "b2fda9c8-7ae1-583d-b5